</Field Guns Equipment>

<overview>
<p>Capellan infantry serve where BattleMechs and armor cannot be spared, which in the resource-constrained CCAF means nearly everywhere. The Xin Sheng movement revitalized the infantry arm alongside every other facet of the Capellan Confederation Armed Forces, giving foot soldiers better equipment and renewed purpose. Mechanized wheeled platoons balance speed and infantry presence, using armored wheeled transports to move troops quickly along the Confederation's road networks. They sacrifice the cross-country capability of tracked vehicles for faster transit between defensive positions. Equipped with laser rifles that offer superior range and armor penetration compared to ballistic weapons, these platoons field one of the most effective personal arms available to conventional infantry, though the weapons are significantly more expensive and require soldiers to carry additional power packs. TAG spotter sections within the platoon carry target acquisition gear that can designate targets for semi-active homing munitions, enabling precision strikes from artillery, aerospace, or missile-equipped units operating beyond visual range.</p>
</overview>

<notes>
Intro date based on re-introduction date of man-portable TAG weapon
</notes>

